   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "CLINICAL SUMMARY - Daniels Green and Barton Clinic\nPatient: Shannon Reid DOB: 08/02/1992 Sex: F MRN: 312765\n\nEncounters:\n 2025-08-09 Lupus BP 115/75 Wt 107\n 2025-04-02 Lupus BP 118/67 Wt 116\n 2024-11-24 Lupus BP 116/65 Wt 113\n 2024-07-17 Lupus BP 117/77 Wt 115\n 2024-03-10 Lupus BP 115/69 Wt 116\n 2023-11-02 Lupus BP 119/69 Wt 111\n 2023-06-25 Lupus BP 129/74 Wt 119\n 2023-02-16 Lupus BP 130/69 Wt 118\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n• Lupus (systemic kind) - currently controlled; on prednisone 20 mg and belimumab 200 mg injections.\n• The patient reports no new symptoms since her last visit and continues to manage her condition effectively. Her activity remains stable, with no signs of organ involvement.\n• Blood pressure readings have been within normal limits at all visits, with the latest reading of 115/75 mmHg on 2025-08-09. Weight has maintained within a healthy range, currently at 107 pounds.\n• The patient is compliant with her medication regimen and continues to take her prednisone and belimumab injections as prescribed.\n• Regular exercise is a part of her lifestyle, with the patient running 3-4 times per week, which has been beneficial for her overall health.\n• Social history reveals the patient currently smokes cigarettes at a rate of one per day, with an honest disclosure. She also consumes alcohol approximately three times per week.\n\nClinical findings:\n• Cardiovascular: Normal blood pressure and heart rate.\n• Respiratory: Normal respiratory rate and clear breath sounds.\n• Musculoskeletal: No joint swelling or tenderness.\n• Neurological: Normal reflexes and sensation.\n• Skin: No rashes or lesions noted.\n• Gastrointestinal: Normal bowel sounds and no abdominal tenderness.\n• Genitourinary: No abnormalities detected.\n• Hematologic: No signs of bleeding or bruising.\n\nContinued Monitoring:\n• Regular follow-up appointments to monitor lupus activity and adjust medications as needed.\n• Ongoing assessment of organ function and potential side effects from medications.\n• Encourage continued exercise and healthy lifestyle habits.\n• Smoking cessation support and resources to reduce tobacco use.\n• Monitoring alcohol consumption to ensure it remains within safe limits.\n\nMedications:\n• Prednisone 20 mg daily\n• Belimumab 200 mg injection every 2 weeks\n\nThe patient remains stable with her lupus under control, adhering to her treatment plan. She is encouraged to maintain her current lifestyle and continue with her prescribed medications. Any changes in her condition or symptoms will be promptly addressed during her follow-up visits.\n"
    }
